Static page vs dynamic page
In nextjs,all pages are static by default
=>Static means us page pr apka data change ni hu rha.Static pages are pages that do not depend on any request-time or changing data.

=>A Page will become dynamic when it depends on data that can change between requests like using (See dynamic page img)
a)searchParams  b)useSearchParams c)fetch d)usePathName e)When you manually make your page dynamic by export const dynamic='force-dynamic'  etc

imp:
Jab ap database sy data fetch kr rhy hu aur wo kisi param/searchparam k upr depend ni ha tu tab b ye apk page ko as a static he treat kry ga.

=>Run command npm run build and see that which pages are static and which are dynamic
See image named "Static vs Dynamic identity",a circle shaped represent static page jab k hum ny in mei db ka data collect kiya ha, while  f keyword represents dynamic page

=>After run "npm run build",now i want to run production command (jo build mainy npm run build kr k bnai ha,usy ab production me run kr du) by using npm run start(production command)

Imp:

=>When you run npm run build, Next.js pre-renders all pages that don’t need changing data — these are static and built once. If a page needs request-time information like searchParams, cookies, or  fetch, Next.js cannot pre-render it, so it becomes a dynamic page and runs on the server every time a user requests it.
=>After run "npm run start",ab hamari build production me ha.mai agr ab apny code me kuch b change kr lo,koi b changes ab reflect ni hu gi kyu k hum ny jis build pr production chlai ha,un mei ye changes ni thi.Agr hum wo changes dikhana chahty ha tu hamai dobara new build bnani hu gi by using "npm run build"
=>When we are in production,hamaray data jo let suppose hamai db sy a rha ha ,us me koi update huti ha tu dynamic page me wo changes reflect hu gi mgr static page me previous data ko he hold rkhy ga which means static page me changes reflect ni hugi.



